---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import Val from '../components/Val.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
const d = site.legalDetails;
const email = site.contact.email;
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Thehraav Counselling collects, uses and protects your personal data, in plain language, and how to ask for it to be deleted."
>
  <p>
    Your privacy matters, especially when you're reaching out for support. This policy explains, in plain language,
    what personal data Thehraav Counselling collects, why, where it's kept, and the choices you have. It's written to
    follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act).
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Thehraav Counselling is the online counselling practice of {site.psychologist.name}, counselling psychologist.
    For this policy, Sarah is responsible for your personal data (the "Data Fiduciary" under the DPDP Act). You can
    contact her at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website itself does not store any of your personal data. There are no accounts and no database.</li>
    <li>When you book, your details go to our booking tool (Cal ID). When you send a message, it goes to Sarah's email.</li>
    <li>We only use your data to arrange and provide your sessions and to reply to you.</li>
    <li>We never sell your data or use it for advertising.</li>
    <li>You can ask to see, correct or delete your data at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Booking details</strong>: your name, email, the time you choose, and any answers you give to the short
      booking questions (for example, what you'd like help with or your preferred language). We use these to schedule
      your session, send confirmations and reminders, and prepare for your first session.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment details</strong>: payments are handled by Razorpay. We see that a payment was made and how much,
      but we never see or store your card, UPI or bank details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form messages</strong>: your name, email and message. We use these only to reply to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>WhatsApp and email messages</strong>: if you contact Sarah this way, your messages and number or email
      address are kept by those services and used only to reply to you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent and intake forms</strong>: after booking, you're sent links to these forms. They help Sarah
      understand your needs and record your consent to counselling.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We rely on your consent to process this data, which you give when you book, send a message or fill in a form. You
    can withdraw your consent at any time by emailing us. This won't affect anything already done, but it may mean we
    can't continue sessions.
  </p>

  <h2>Where your data is stored</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of trusted services to run the practice. Each has its own privacy policy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cal ID</strong> (booking and calendar), which stores booking details and booking-question answers</li>
    <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> (payments), which processes payments for paid sessions</li>
    <li><strong>Formspree</strong> (contact form), which passes your message to Sarah's email</li>
    <li><strong>Microsoft Outlook</strong> (email), where messages and booking notifications are received</li>
    <li><strong><Val v={d.intakeFormService} /></strong> (consent and intake forms)</li>
    <li><strong><Val v={d.videoService} /></strong> (video sessions). Calls happen live on this service.</li>
    <li><strong>Railway</strong> (website hosting), which may keep basic technical logs such as IP addresses for security</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these services may store data outside India. We choose providers with strong security practices, and we
    only share what each one needs to do its job.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website doesn't use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. When you open the booking calendar, Cal ID
    may set cookies needed for booking to work.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your data only as long as needed to provide your sessions and meet professional and legal record-keeping
    duties, which is usually <Val v={d.retention} />. After that, it's deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the DPDP Act, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask what personal data we hold about you and how it's used</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct or update your data</li>
    <li>Ask us to delete your data (unless we must keep it by law)</li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent</li>
    <li>Nominate someone to exercise these rights for you in case of death or incapacity</li>
    <li>Raise a concern or complaint with us</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to ask for your data to be deleted</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with the subject line "Data request", and tell us what you'd like us
    to do. We may ask you to confirm your identity. We'll respond within <Val v={d.responseTime} />.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a concern about how your data is handled, please contact us first at
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. If you're not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Data
    Protection Board of India.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we make important changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</LegalLayout>
